(D2 — Discrepancy 2 repro (wrong-value half): a `map` parameter's `'s size`
 and `'s length` both return -1, while the same map read at top level
 returns 2. Element access through the parameter (`lookup's "ann"`) is
 correct, so it is the size/length property specifically that is wrong.
 LANGUAGE.md:724-725 says a typed parameter "supports the same properties
 and operations as a top-level variable of that type".
 The `a float called pad` line is load-bearing: without a float somewhere
 in the program the same code does not assemble at all — see D2b.vox.
